      "options": {
        "content": "### Useful Explore queries\n\nPrometheus\n- `sum by (model, token_type) (max_over_time(codex_turn_token_usage_sum[$__range]))`\n- `topk(20, sum by (kind) (max_over_time(codex_websocket_event_total[$__range])))`\n- `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, tool) (max_over_time(codex_tool_call_duration_ms_milliseconds_bucket[$__range])))`\n- `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, cache) (max_over_time(codex_mcp_tools_list_duration_ms_milliseconds_bucket[$__range])))`\n\nLoki\n- `{service_name=~\"codex_exec|codex_cli_rs\"} | event_name=\"codex.user_prompt\"`\n- `{service_name=~\"codex_exec|codex_cli_rs\"} | event_name=\"codex.tool_result\"`\n- `{service_name=~\"codex_exec|codex_cli_rs\"} | event_name=\"codex.sse_event\" | event_kind=\"response.completed\"`\n\nNotes\n- The top token cards are adapted from the SigNoz Codex dashboard pattern: `Total`, `Input`, `Output`, `Cached`, and `Cache Utilization Rate`.\n- Use `Conversation ID` with an exact value or regex to drill into one session.\n- This dashboard is snapshot-oriented: the Prometheus panels use `max_over_time(...)` so totals remain visible after a run finishes.\n- MCP panels currently show discovery and cache telemetry. No `mcp__*` tool-result events were observed in this local dataset yet.\n- Codex Loki stream labels differ by CLI/runtime version. This dashboard matches both `codex_exec` and `codex_cli_rs`.\n- Loki stores OTLP attributes as structured metadata with dots converted to underscores, so `event.name` becomes `event_name` and `conversation.id` becomes `conversation_id`.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
